WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.630
An oil platform.

2
00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.530
A desalination plant.

3
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.410
A lithium brine field.

4
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.610
A battery production line.

5
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:11.750
Lithium demand rose nearly
30 per cent in 2024.

6
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:16.550
Nearly 3 billion people live in areas
where total water storage is projected to

7
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.630
decline.

8
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.170
And in two International
Energy Agency scenarios,

9
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:26.310
world electricity demand rises
by about 40 per cent to 2035.

10
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.630
So will the world run short
of energy, water or metals,

11
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.810
or will something change first?

12
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:36.730
In this mission, you'll see why
agencies model several futures,

13
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.530
not one forecast.

14
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.230
Then you'll compare
possible futures for energy,

15
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.190
water and metal ores.

16
00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:46.210
Your mission: decide
which future for energy,

17
00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:49.160
water and metals the
evidence best supports.
